cite1†Sign in L109: \nL110: cite60†Sign up L111: \nL112: Appearance settings\nL113: You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: ### Uh oh!\nL115: \nL116: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL117: \nL118: cite61†w3c / cite62†csswg-drafts Public\nL119: \nL120:   * cite63†Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings\nL121:   * cite63†Fork 811 L122:   * cite63†Star L123: \nL124:   * cite62†Code L125:   * cite64†Issues 4.5k L126:   * cite65†Pull requests 130 L127:   * cite66†Discussions L128:   * cite67†Actions L129:   * cite68†Projects L130:   * cite69†Security and quality 0 L131:   * cite70†Insights L132: \nL133: Additional navigation options\nL134: # [css-logical-1] [css-cascade-3] The all shorthand probably shouldn't set logical properties. #1898\nL135: \nL136: New issue\nL137: \nL138: Copy link\nL139: \nL140: New issue\nL141: \nL142: Copy link\nL143: \nL144: Closed\nL145: \nL146: cite71†#2516 L147: \nL148: Closed\nL149: \nL150: cite72†[css-logical-1] [css-cascade-3] The all shorthand probably shouldn't set logical properties. #1898\nL151: \nL152: cite71†#2516 L153: \nL154: Copy link\nL155: \nL156: Labels\nL157: \nL158: cite73†cssom-1Current Work Current Work\nL159: ## Description\nL160: \nL161: cite74†emilio L162: \nL163: opened cite75†on Oct 23, 2017 L164: \nL165: Issue body actions\nL166: \nL167: Or if it should, order of the expansion of `all` should be specified.\nL168: \nL169: From cite76†https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-3/#all-shorthand†drafts.csswg.org :\nL170: \nL171: > The all property is a shorthand that resets all CSS properties except direction and unicode-bidi. It only accepts the CSS-wide keywords.\nL172: This includes logical properties, and this is a problem because that means that it produces unexpected results when used from CSSOM (where the position a property declaration appears on matters).\nL173: \nL174: In particular, we came across cite77†https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1410028†bugzilla.mozilla.org , which happens because of the internal order the properties are reset.\nL175: \nL176: In particular, it's not the same if `all` expands to:\nL177: \nL178:     `padding-inline-start: initial;\nL179:     padding-left: initial;\nL180:     `\nL181: that if it expands the other way around.\nL182: i.e., this two pieces of code should be equivalent:\nL183: \nL184:     <!doctype html>\nL185:     <script>\nL186:     let setStyle = (el, props) => {\nL187:       for (prop in props)\nL188:         el.style.setProperty(prop, props[prop]);\nL189:     };\nL190: \nL191:     let logical = document.createElement('div');\nL192:     let physical = document.createElement('div');\nL193: \nL194:     setStyle(physical, {\nL195:       all: 'initial',\nL196:       'background-color': 'blue',\nL197:       display: 'block',\nL198:       width: '100px',\nL199:       height: '100px',\nL200:       padding: '10px'\nL201:     });\nL202:     setStyle(logical, {\nL203:       all: 'initial',\nL204:       'background-color': 'blue',\nL205:       display: 'block',\nL206:       width: '100px',\nL207:       height: '100px',\nL208:       'padding-inline-start': '10px',\nL209:       'padding-inline-end': '10px',\nL210:       'padding-block-start': '10px',\nL211:       'padding-block-end': '10px'\nL212:     });\nL213: \nL214:     document.documentElement.appendChild(physical);\nL215:     document.documentElement.appendChild(logical);\nL216:     </script>\nL217: But they aren't in current browsers.\nL218: \nL219: Reactions are currently unavailable\nL220: ## Metadata\nL221: \nL222: ## Metadata\nL223: \nL224: ### Assignees\nL225: \nL226: No one assigned\nL227: \nL228: ### Labels\nL229: \nL230: cite73†cssom-1Current Work