operties #6894\nL146: \nL147: Copy link\nL148: \nL149: Labels\nL150: \nL151: cite73†cssom-1Current Work Current Work\nL152: ## Description\nL153: \nL154: cite74†cdoublev L155: \nL156: opened cite75†on Dec 16, 2021 L157: \nL158: Issue body actions\nL159: The cite76†specified order of declarations†drafts.csswg.org define that shorthand properties [are] expanded into their longhand properties, in canonical order, and a cite77†general principle of serialization†drafts.csswg.org is that if certain component values can appear in any order without changing the meaning of the value (a pattern typically represented by a double bar || in the value syntax), reorder the component values to use the canonical order of component values as given in the property definition table.\nL160: When setting `background` to a single `<final-bg-layer>`, Chrome serializes the component values in the order derived from `<bg-layer>` and append `<bg-color>` at the end, while Firefox serializes in another order.\nL161: \nL162:     style.background = 'url(\"bg.jpg\") left 10% / 100px 100% no-repeat fixed content-box padding-box red'\nL163:     console.log(style.background)\nL164:     // Chrome: same as input\nL165:     // Firefox: red url(\"bg.jpg\") no-repeat fixed left 10% / 100px 100% content-box padding-box\nL166: The motivation of this request is two fold. It would be also handy to be able to extract a list of shorthands from eg. cite78†`w3c/webref` (see cite79†#2921 ). Using this tool, I can extract a list of shorthands by searching for `individual` or `shorthand` in the `initial` or `computed value` fields, but there are some inconsistencies between specifications and I'm not sure that this method is 100% accurate.\nL167: \nL168: Therefore a new definition field value, eg. `shorthand for`, would answer both parts of this request.\nL169: Related: cite80†#5741 .\nL170: \nL171: Reactions are currently unavailable\nL172: ## Metadata\nL173: \nL174: ## Metadata\nL175: \nL176: ### Assignees\nL177: \nL178: No one assigned\nL179: \nL180: ### Labels\nL181: \nL182: cite73†cssom-1Current Work Current Work\nL183: \nL184: ### Type\nL185: \nL186: No type\nL187: \nL188: ### Projects\nL189: \nL190: No projects\nL191: \nL192: ### Milestone\nL193: \nL194: No milestone\nL195: \nL196: ### Relationships\nL197: \nL198: None yet\nL199: \nL200: ### Development\nL201: \nL202: No branches or pull requests\nL203: \nL204: ## Issue actions\nL205: \nL206:   * cite81†Image†github.githubassets.com Open in GitHub Copilot app\nL207: \nL208: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1233view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1410028\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1410028: Cache miss\n"
